Experiment 1(b): Scale EC2 Instance by Changing Instance Type
Aim

To increase or decrease CPU and RAM resources of an EC2 instance by modifying the instance type.

Procedure
Step 1: Open EC2 Dashboard
Go to EC2 → Instances.
Select the required EC2 instance.
Step 2: Stop the Instance
Click:
Instance State → Stop Instance
Wait until instance status becomes Stopped.
Step 3: Change Instance Type
Click:
Actions → Instance Settings → Change Instance Type
Select a higher/lower instance type.
Example:
t2.micro → t2.small
Step 4: Apply Changes
Click Apply or Save.
Step 5: Restart Instance
Click:
Instance State → Start Instance
Step 6: Verify New Configuration
Open instance details.
Check updated:
vCPU
RAM
Performance
Observation
Instance stopped and restarted successfully.
CPU and RAM configuration changed according to selected instance type.
Result

Successfully scaled the EC2 instance by changing the instance type and increasing/decreasing CPU and RAM resources.
